('98429710-dc7d-589c-a7a3-6314408abcd4', 'CF_RE_01', 'I had promised to help my husband''s family move on a Saturday when I was exhausted. I went, stayed until the end, and did not mention how tired I was. A client called with a better offer the same afternoon I had promised my husband I would be at the school event. I turned it down, told my husband about it later, and felt no regret.', NULL, 93, 'christformed', NULL, 66, 124, '2026-10-03T12:44:04.000Z'),
('7954e006-8aac-51dc-af86-a43a529a718e', 'ON_RE_01', 'Money decisions mostly happen on my side. my husband finds out through a statement or a passing comment, and I have not wanted to change that. I accepted an invitation for both of us without checking. When my husband was surprised, I said it was easier than going back and forth.', NULL, 41, 'awakening', NULL, 51, 72, '2026-10-03T12:45:16.000Z'),
('b6e18815-d342-5f84-a5d7-be24309c6f62', 'SL_RE_01', 'I do a lot for my husband, and I notice when it is not acknowledged. I try not to bring it up, and it comes out in small remarks. I helped my husband with a move, but I mentioned afterward how much of my weekend it took. They heard it, and I wish I had not said it.', NULL, 69, 'growing', NULL, 58, 173, '2026-10-03T12:48:04.000Z'),
('656a0d7e-4032-55cd-a2a7-fe49ee5f8380', 'IN_RE_01', 'I share most things openly, but there is one old failure I have never fully explained. my husband has sensed it, and I have not opened that door. I told my husband about a fear I had carried for years. I almost stopped halfway, but I finished and I am glad I did.', NULL, 77, 'rooted', NULL, 53, 135, '2026-10-03T12:50:08.000Z'),
('712ae374-e82f-5bde-aa2f-a1873cbcdc22', 'TC_RE_01', 'I am honest when asked directly. When something is bothering me, it tends to come out as irritation rather than words. I needed to tell my husband I was uncomfortable lending money to their cousin. I joked about it first and said it seriously only days later.', NULL, 50, 'growing', NULL, 47, 107, '2026-10-03T12:52:24.000Z'),
('970b40d8-c1d1-5720-a777-06296152c62e', 'CR_RE_01', 'I usually repair things eventually, after a stretch of coldness. Pride gets in the way more than I would like to admit. After our argument I knew I should apologise, but I waited until my husband moved first. It took two days, which was longer than either of us wanted.', NULL, 60, 'growing', NULL, 50, 85, '2026-10-03T12:55:11.000Z'),
('27bb4318-4521-5cd8-a5d7-0042b7fbeabe', 'MH_RE_01', 'I usually speak well of my husband. Once I rolled my eyes in front of others and felt it immediately. I apologised in private. I was frustrated with my husband and still spoke respectfully. Later I told them I had been stressed and apologised for my tone.', NULL, 75, 'rooted', NULL, 47, 153, '2026-10-03T12:56:24.000Z'),
('dbedf815-f341-5312-a9db-8104c80facb7', 'SV_RE_01', 'Our plans are real but vague. I assume my husband pictures the same future, and I have never checked. We both say we want some land and a growing family. I have not actually asked my husband where, or what they would give up to get there.', NULL, 55, 'growing', NULL, 47, 93, '2026-10-03T12:58:20.000Z'),
('e6d9024a-da10-5f37-a19c-c027e21d1cd4', 'X_RE_01', 'I think Daniel would say we are closer than I would. I have learned not to push when he withdraws, and I miss being let in more than I say.', NULL, 64, 'growing', NULL, 30, 136, '2026-10-03T13:00:03.000Z')
